<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 13 January, from 532 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">532 <span class="tih-ago">1,494 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nika riots break out in Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rival chariot-racing factions united against Emperor Justinian and burned much of the city. Urged by Empress Theodora not to flee, Justinian had the rising crushed, with some 30,000 killed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1128 <span class="tih-ago">898 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Council of Troyes endorses the Knights Templar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A church council at Troyes, led by a papal legate and inspired by Bernard of Clairvaux, approved a rule for the Knights Templar. The order of warrior monks became a major force in the Crusades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusades">Crusades</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/united-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1847 <span class="tih-ago">179 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Cahuenga ends the fighting in California</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Californio leader Andrés Pico and John C. Frémont signed an informal capitulation near Los Angeles. It ended hostilities in California, which Mexico ceded to the United States in 1848.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1898 <span class="tih-ago">128 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Émile Zola publishes 'J'accuse...!'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Zola's open letter in L'Aurore accused the French army of convicting the Jewish officer Alfred Dreyfus wrongly and covering up the truth. It turned the Dreyfus affair into a national crisis.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1915 <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Avezzano earthquake devastates central Italy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 6.7 earthquake struck the Abruzzo region, killing about 30,000 people. In Avezzano itself almost all of the population perished.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1942 <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry Ford patents a plastic car body</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry Ford received a patent for a car body built from plastic panels on a tubular frame, part of his experiments with materials derived from soybeans. Wartime restrictions ended the project.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1968 <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Johnny Cash performs at Folsom State Prison</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Johnny Cash played two shows for inmates at Folsom Prison in California, recorded for a live album. 'At Folsom Prison' revived his career and became one of the best-known albums in country music.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1991 <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet troops storm the Vilnius television tower</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces attacked unarmed crowds defending Lithuanian broadcasting sites in Vilnius, killing 14 civilians. The violence strengthened support for Baltic independence at home and abroad.</p></div></li></ol>
